AB  - The GitHub Actions documentation is a vital resource for educating developers about the most prominent Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) platform in the open-source community. Although CI/CD accelerates the software development process, it poses a significant risk to the software supply chain, as demonstrated by recurring attacks on open-source GitHub Actions dependencies and workflows. While previous work has prioritized detecting vulnerable CI/CD workflows, we assess, from a preventive perspective, whether the official documentation provides security guidance for secure CI/CD. In this work, we extract 459 security advice items from the GitHub documentation using a Large Language Model-based few-shot approach. We then apply the SAcoding methodology to the OWASP Top 10 CI/CD security risk framework to identify actionable recommendations. GitHub and OWASP align on credential and configuration-based weaknesses; however GitHub does not effectively utilize its visual alerts to inform developers.
ER  - 

