AB  - With the continuous integration of a large number of renewable energy generators into power systems, their impact on grid voltage stability has become inevitable. To address voltage fluctuations and over-limit issues caused by the integration of renewable energy sources, this paper proposes a voltage optimization method for power systems based on artificial intelligence algorithms. First, historical renewable energy output data and historical load data from the power system are collected and used to train a predictive model with machine learning algorithms. Based on this model, input data from typical time periods are used to obtain output datasets, which serve as inputs for voltage optimization. Then, a deep reinforcement learning algorithm is employed to select the optimal voltage regulation actions by maximizing the reward function, adjusting the corresponding voltage control devices accordingly. Finally, to validate the proposed method, simulations are conducted on an improved IEEE 33-bus system, incorporating wind, solar, and other voltage regulation devices. The results demonstrate that the proposed approach significantly reduces the average voltage deviation of grid nodes and effectively increases the voltage magnitude of over-limit nodes. This confirms the superior performance of the proposed method in voltage optimization control, providing effective support for voltage stability and enhancing the grid’s voltage regulation capability.
ER  - 

