AB  - With the continuous integration and innovation of digital information technology and education, automatic evaluation system, as an intelligent educational tool, is being widely used in various examinations and teaching activities in foreign language teaching. However, at present, the automatic evaluation system still has some shortcomings in processing accuracy, consistency of grading standards and technical stability, which is difficult to meet the practical application needs of colleges and universities. In this regard, based on the current situation, this paper will deeply explore the application feasibility of artificial intelligence, that is, deep neural network technology in this field, and propose a brand-new subjective question evaluation model, aiming at improving the practical performance of subjective question evaluation system. Practice has proved that this model takes CNN-LSTM as the core and combines natural language processing technology, which can automatically extract complex features from a large number of text data and deal with nonlinear problems through multi-layer structure, thus achieving more accurate scoring. At the same time, with the efficient computing power of deep neural network, large-scale subjective question data can be processed quickly, which achieves the purpose of improving the efficiency of subjective question evaluation, and then promotes the informationization and intelligent development of foreign language teaching mode.
