AB  - To Analyze the Accuracy of climatic changes in real time using machine learning techniques such as Novel Stochastic Gradient Descent and Naive Bayes. Novel Stochastic Gradient Descent is utilized to determine the weather patterns and the accuracy is contrasted with Naive Bayes. The accuracy to predict the weather forecast on a sample size of 200 for each algorithm. For the SPSS analysis, G power of 0.95, CI (continuous Integration) of 95%, and alpha of 0.29 is used. As a result, Novel Stochastic Gradient Descent 94.25% is more accurate than Naive Bayes (92.78%). The accuracy significance value is 0.18. This demonstrates that there is no statistical significance among the two methods. The Novel Stochastic Gradient Descent achieved accuracy of 94.25%, better than Naive Bayes (92.78%) for the chosen Weather prediction dataset.
