AB  - The software testing process is a critical phase in the software development lifecycle, aimed at systematically evaluating and validating the functionality, efficacy, and dependability of software applications to ensure they meet specified requirements and deliver high-quality user experiences. Nevertheless, despite its significance, the software testing process often faces challenges like high time consumption and resource demands, which can impact project schedules and budgets if not managed effectively. In this paper, a hybrid deep learning-based framework for improving intelligent decision-making in software testing processes is proposed. At first, the input data are taken via Intelligent Test Management System. To implement this, the input data is preprocessed utlizing Fast Resampled Iterative Filtering, which performs error correction, removes duplicate data, handles missing values, and encodes categorical variables in the dataset. Then, the pre-processed data is provided to the Signed Cumulative Distribution Transform for extracting semantic and categorical information from test specifications such as descriptions, procedures, and quality attributes. After that, the extracted features are given to the Progressive Graph Convolutional Networks, which forecasts the Continuous Integration configuration for each test case. Finally, the Multi-feature Attention Convolutional Neural Network is utilized to categorize whether every test case should be automated or implemented manually, thereby improving test accuracy, minimizing effort, and optimizing software testing efficiency. Then the proposed method is implemented in python and the performance metrics like Accuracy, Precision, F1-Score and Rate of Curve are analysed. The performance of the proposed approach attains highest accuracy for automated and manual. The role of artificial intelligence and machine learning in software testing and mitigating noise in quantum software testing using ML methods respectively.
ER  - 

