AB  - As software development advances, maintaining reliable Continuous Integration (CI) pipelines is essential because build failures can delay releases, raise costs, and reduce code quality. This paper presents a system that predicts CI build failures using deep learning and Machine Learning Operations (MLOps). The system employs Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) networks optimized with Genetic Algorithms (GA) to capture temporal build patterns. A web-based platform, CIFlow, offers user management, repository integration, workflow control, and Artificial Intelligence (AI) model monitoring. Built on a microservices architecture and deployed on Kubernetes, it ensures scalability and automation, while Development, Security, and Operations (DevSecOps) and GitOps enhance security and efficiency. Experimental results show high Area Under the Curve (AUC) scores, proving the system's effectiveness in reducing build failures and improving CI pipeline reliability.
