AB  - In today's digital era, analyzing user behaviour through mobile usage data is essential for enhancing user engagement and delivering personalized services. Integrating machine learning with DevOps practices enables automated, scalable, and real-time behaviour analysis systems. This framework employs machine learning models such as Random Forests, Decision Trees, and Neural Networks to classify user activity based on features like screen time, app usage frequency, and behavioural patterns. The models are trained on preprocessed and feature-engineered datasets to predict categories like Work-Oriented, Entertainment-Focused, or Balanced Users. The proposed system achieves high performance with accuracy exceeding 90 %, supported by precision and recall metrics that confirm its robustness in behavioural classification. Combined with Git-based version control, Jenkins-driven CI/CD, and AWS EC2 deployment, the framework ensures continuous integration, deployment, and scalability for real-time insights. It demonstrates a novel end-to-end MLOps approach that seamlessly automates model training, testing, and cloud deployment for dynamic behaviour profiling.
