AB  - Machine learning offers transformative potential for administrative decision-making, particularly in complex visa application processes. This research introduces a sophisticated Machine Learning Operations (ML-Ops) pipeline that leverages advanced ensemble learning techniques to predict United States visa application outcomes with unprecedented accuracy. By integrating Random Forest, XG-Boost, and Gradient Boosting algorithms, the study develops a robust predictive model that comprehensively analyzes multidimensional applicant features including geographical origin, educational qualifications, professional experience, and demographic characteristics. The proposed pipeline implements rigorous Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) principles, enabling automated model retraining, precise performance monitoring, and systematic drift detection. Achieving a remarkable F1-score of [score], the research demonstrates significant improvements over the traditional manual assessment methodologies. This groundbreaking method not only advances visa application processing but also establishes a critical framework for integrating intelligent, data-driven decision-making systems in complex administrative contexts.
