AB  - The rapid proliferation of Internet of Things (IoT) devices has resulted in unprecedented volumes of heterogeneous data streams, creating new challenges for secure, compliant, and scalable data management. Traditional DevSecOps practices provide continuous integration and delivery pipelines, yet they are not inherently equipped to enforce dynamic compliance across multicloud ecosystems. This paper presents an automated complianceaware DevSecOps framework for AI-driven IoT data streams, integrating cloud-native machine learning services across Amazon Web Services (AWS), Google Cloud Platform (GCP), and Microsoft Azure. The framework introduces a compliance orchestration layer that continuously monitors regulatory requirements such as HIPAA, GDPR, and ISO 27001, embedding them directly into data ingestion, transformation, and analytics pipelines. Cloud-native ML models are deployed to detect anomalies, classify workloads, and adapt security policies in real time, while monitoring ensures interoperability and resilience across providers. Experimental evaluation demonstrates that the proposed framework achieves significant reductions in compliance drift, improves detection of misconfigurations, and maintains low-latency processing for high-velocity IoT data streams. By unifying DevSecOps automation with compliance-driven machine learning in multi-cloud environments, this work provides a resilient foundation for enterprises seeking to operationalize secure, regulation-aligned IoT analytics at scale.
ER  - 

